---@class posthog.notebooks.NotebookKernelConfigResponse
---@field cpu_cores? number|distilled.Null Configured CPU cores; null means the default applies.
---@field memory_gb? number|distilled.Null Configured memory in GB; null means the default applies.
---@field idle_timeout_seconds? number|distilled.Null Configured maximum sandbox lifetime in seconds; null means the default.
---@field restarted boolean True when this call restarted a live kernel to apply a new size. Restarting discards every materialized dataframe, so cells that referenced one must run again.
---@field restart_required boolean True when a kernel is live and this call did not restart it, so the running sandbox may not match the saved config. A resize restarts the kernel and reports False on success, or True if that restart fails. An idle-timeout change and a no-op on a live kernel also report True.
---@field hourly_price number What this sandbox shape costs per hour in USD while it is alive, at this region's rates. It tracks the running sandbox while a kernel is live, otherwise the configured shape. After a failed resize this stays the running sandbox's rate, not the size that failed to apply.
---@field preset_key? string|distilled.Null Compute preset the configured shape matches, or null when it was tuned by hand.

